# Header Footer Code conventions

## Purpose

HFCM-style sitewide HTML / CSS / JS snippets for Grav 2 Admin Next: list + edit UI, enable/disable, frontend and/or backend injection, header/footer location, optional JS defer/async.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `header-footer-code.php` | Events: API routes, sidebar, plugin page, floating widget, front inject |
| `classes/SnippetRepository.php` | YAML CRUD under `user/data/header-footer-code/snippets.yaml` (runtime data — do not commit site data from this repo) |
| `classes/SnippetInjector.php` | Front-end Asset Manager + HTML output injection |
| `classes/Api/HeaderFooterCodeController.php` | REST CRUD + `/active` |
| `admin-next/pages/header-footer-code.js` | List + edit Admin Next page (CodeMirror) |
| `admin-next/widgets/header-footer-code.js` | autoLoad backend injector (`showFab: false`) |
| `assets/admin/page.css` | Admin list/edit styles (lazy-linked by page JS) |

## CSS

Keep admin styles in `assets/admin/page.css`. Prefer `hfc-*` class names with single hyphens (no BEM `__` / `--`). Do not add inline `<style>` in JS unless the user asks.

## Injection rules

- **Frontend:** `onAssetsInitialized` (CSS/JS) + `onOutputGenerated` (HTML). Skip admin and API routes.
- **Backend:** floating widget with `autoLoad: true`, `showFab: false`; inject at module load (Admin2 may not mount the element when FAB is hidden).
- CSS always goes in `<head>` even if location is footer (document in UI help text).
- No PHP snippet type. Snippets run as-is — keep the UI warning.

## Admin Next

- Sidebar route: `/plugin/header-footer-code`
- Permissions: `admin.header-footer-code.read` / `.write`
- Delete confirms via `window.__GRAV_DIALOGS` — never native `confirm()`
- API auth header: `X-API-Token`

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).
